lontana":"en","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Coined by Israeli politician David Remez, a calque of German Seemanschaft or calque of English seamanship, from יַמַּאי (yamáy, “a seaman”) + ־וּת (-ut, “-ness, -ity”), the first part from יָם (yam, “sea”) + ־ַאי (áy, “-ian, -eer”, denoting a profession or occupation.)."},{"parola":"ישיבה","traslitterazione":"yeshivá","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"no","significato":"sitting","termine_origine":"Sitzung","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Sitzung","categoria":"calco"}],"lontana":"de","ambiti":["religione"],"via":"","testo":"Action noun of יָשַׁב (yasháv, “to sit”). The modern, secularized sense as \"board meeting\" might be a semantic loan from German Sitzung."},{"parola":"כלב ים","traslitterazione":"kélev-yam","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"no","significato":"seal (a pinniped (Pinnipedia), particularly an earless seal (true seal) or eared seal)","termine_origine":"Seehund","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Seehund","categoria":"calco"}],"lontana":"de","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Calque of German Seehund. In the Revival literature era there were authors appending the meaning \"shark\" to it, in analogy to Arabic كَلْب الْبَحْر (kalb al-baḥr) or French chien-de-mer, but the \"seal\" sense eventually prevailed."},{"parola":"כלור","traslitterazione":"klór","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"chlorine (a toxic, green, gaseous chemical element (symbol Cl) with an atomic number of 17)","termine_origine":"Chlor","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Chlor","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"chlore","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"chlorine","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"χλωρός","traslitterazione":"khlōrós","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Likely via German Chlor or French chlore, from English chlorine, itself derived from Ancient Greek χλωρός (khlōrós, “pale green”) + -ine. Compare also Yiddish כלאָר (khlor), Polish chlor and Russian хлор (xlor) for the phonetic influence."},{"parola":"ליתוגרפיה","traslitterazione":"litografya","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"lithography","termine_origine":"Lithographie","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Lithographie","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Ultimately from German Lithographie, a modern coinage from Ancient Greek λίθος (líthos, “stone”) + γράφειν (gráphein, “to write”)."},{"parola":"מדעי הרוח","traslitterazione":"mad'éi ha-rúach","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"no","significato":"humanities (the branch of learning that includes the arts, classics, philosophy and history etc.)","termine_origine":"Geisteswissenschaften","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Geisteswissenschaften","categoria":"calco"}],"lontana":"de","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"מַדְּעֵי (“sciences of”) + הַ־ (ha-, “the”) + רוּחַ (rúach, “spirit”), calque of German Geisteswissenschaften."},{"parola":"מחנה ריכוז","traslitterazione":"makhané rikúz","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"no","significato":"A concentration camp.","termine_origine":"Konzentrationslager","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Konzentrationslager","categoria":"calco"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"concentration camp","categoria":"calco"}],"lontana":"en","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Calque of German Konzentrationslager, itself a calque of English concentration camp."},{"parola":"מטריצה","traslitterazione":"matrítsa","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"matrix (all senses